    {
      "type": "listeningComp",
      "audioUrl": "/audio/unit-26/testimonio-puerto.mp3",
      "transcript": "Yo trabajo en el puerto desde niño. Ese hombre ha venido todos los días durante tres semanas. Ha llegado siempre a las seis de la mañana y se ha sentado en el mismo banco, mirando el mar. Nunca ha hablado con nadie. Un día le he preguntado qué esperaba y me ha dicho una sola cosa: «Un barco que ya no va a llegar». Todavía no sé qué significa.",
      "translation": "I have worked at the port since I was a boy. That man has come every day for three weeks. He has always arrived at six in the morning and has sat on the same bench, looking at the sea. He has never spoken to anyone. One day I asked him what he was waiting for and he told me only one thing: 'A ship that is not going to arrive now.' I still do not know what it means.",
